  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-3,-1)$ is $(-3,-1)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-1,3)$ is $[-2,2)$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-3,-1)\\cup [-2,2)=(-3,2),$ which can also be written as \n\n$$\n-3<f(x)<2.\n$$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=-3$ and $y=2$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use \"less than\" $(<)$ instead of \"less than or equal to\" $(\\le )$ at these endpoints.",
